# CODEOWNERS — the enforcement half of CONTRIBUTING.md's second-maintainer rule.
#
# These two directories are the files relay's own supervisor executes, sometimes
# while a relay session is the one proposing the change. A missed review here is
# a corrupted overnight run, not a filed bug.
#
# This file only has teeth when the repository ALSO enables, on the default
# branch: "Require a pull request before merging" + "Require review from Code
# Owners". Without that setting this file is advisory.
#
# Consequence to accept deliberately: GitHub does not let an author approve
# their own pull request. With a single code owner, a change to these paths
# cannot be merged by that owner alone — which is precisely the rule
# CONTRIBUTING.md states. Adding a second maintainer here is what unblocks it.

/plugins/relay/scripts/    @cptnbg
/plugins/relay/hooks/      @cptnbg
